{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.le_of_le_join","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.le_of_le_join","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L219-L227","doc":"**The finite window.** Contrapositive of `join_lt_of_lt_sum`: a pair that matches the\nincumbent `V` lies in `a + b ≤ L`, so the maximisation is over a finite set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.join_lt_of_lt_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.join_lt_of_lt_sum","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L204-L217","doc":"**The reduction.** With `f` and `g` bounded above by `B` and `h` below `V - 2B` past `L`,\na pair whose sum exceeds `L` cannot reach `V`.\n\nNothing here knows what `f`, `g` or `h` are: it is the observation that a bounded-plus-bounded\nsum cannot rescue a term that has fallen far enough. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.sum_ghatBot_frame_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.sum_ghatBot_frame_bound","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L183-L202","doc":"**Multi-row `Ghat_bot` frame bound.**\nSumming `ghatBot_frame_bound` across a displacement profile `u : ι → ℕ` bounds the total\nframe-linearised excess by `∑ a, (u a : ℝ) * ghatBot e δ b0 a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.ghatBot_frame_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.ghatBot_frame_bound","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L145-L181","doc":"**Finite-sum `Ghat_bot` frame assembly (`qou-zx9y`).**\nFor any finite frame `b0 : ι → ℕ`, displacing row `a` by `D` (within the gaps `b0 j - b0 a` of rows\nabove `a`) changes the sum of its one-body potential and its pairwise interactions with the rest of\nthe frame by at most `(D : ℝ) * ghatBot e δ b0 a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.ghatBot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.ghatBot","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L133-L143","doc":"**Per-row bottom-frame slope `Ghat_bot`.**\nAt frame row `a` with undisplaced positions `b0 : ι → ℕ`, `ghatBot` combines:\n1. the one-body slope `e (b0 a + 1)`,\n2. the gain from rows strictly below `a` (`b0 j < b0 a`), where the gap `b0 a - b0 j` widens, and\n3. the loss from rows strictly above `a` (`b0 a < b0 j`), where the gap `b0 j - b0 a` narrows.\n\nIt is a signed difference, not a sum (`qou-zx9y`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.one_body_sub_le_mul_of_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.one_body_sub_le_mul_of_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L117-L131","doc":"**One-body linearisation.** If the upward steps of the one-body potential `fi` are `e (m + 1)`\nand `e` is antitone, then displacing a row from `b` to `b + D` gains at most `D * e (b + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.sub_le_neg_mul_of_antitone_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.sub_le_neg_mul_of_antitone_step","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L95-L115","doc":"**Linearisation, downward.** The same inequality on the other side of `a`: climbing `D`\nplaces *gains* at least `D` copies of the first step, so the signed statement is uniform.\n\nThis is the half an agent drops, and dropping it is what makes the bound in the `REV_n` arc\ndiverge — the negative pair terms are exactly what stops a long alternating displacement from\ncollecting the largest step over and over at linear cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.sub_le_mul_of_antitone_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SearchCoercivity.sub_le_mul_of_antitone_step","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SearchCoercivity.lean#L76-L93","doc":"**Linearisation, upward.** If the downward steps `δ` of `e` are antitone, then dropping `D`\nplaces costs at most `D` copies of the *first* step.\n\n`δ` antitone is the discrete form of \"`e` is convex decreasing\": later steps are no larger than\nearlier ones, so the first one dominates the average. ","signatureChunk":0}]}